# Canonical commit identity for this repository.
#
# Every commit on `main` is authored by GitHub's squash-merge using the merging
# account's profile identity, which was a personal name/address rather than the
# project identity. This map makes `git log --use-mailmap` (the default for
# `git shortlog`, `git blame`, and GitHub's own contributor views) report the
# canonical identity instead, without rewriting a single commit.
#
# Format: <canonical name> <canonical email> <commit name> <commit email>
#
# Note: a mailmap must name the old identity in order to redirect it, so the
# previous address necessarily remains visible in this file. Mailmap fixes
# attribution and documents provenance; it does not erase the old address from
# the repository. Only a history rewrite does that — see
# docs/repository-identity.md for that decision.

DriivAIDev <will@driivai.com> <williamnunlist@gmail.com>
DriivAIDev <will@driivai.com> Benji Franclin <williamnunlist@gmail.com>
